            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Square both sides and check both candidates in the original equation; only ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "x=4",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " is valid.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Squaring both sides gives\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=(x-2)^2\\\\x^2-5x+4&=0\\\\(x-1)(x-4)&=0\\\\x&=1\\text{ or }4.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=1$, $\\sqrt{1}=1$ but $1-2=-1$, so reject $x=1$.\n\nAt $x=4$, $\\sqrt{4}=2$ and $4-2=2$, so $x=4$ satisfies the original equation.\n\nTherefore there is one solution.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
